#### Presence/absence

Pyseer code to evaluate the association between gene presence/absence data (binary and continuous).

pyseer_results_Glucose_maf05_PA.txt

The phenotypic trait was the continuous anthrone values, where each phenotypic value is the Glucose/OD600. We ran a linear mixed model (lmm). In the glucose phenotype, the population structure was accounted for as the kinship matrix 

pyseer --lmm --phenotypes Data_input/Glucose_phenotype_pyseer.tsv \
  --pres Data_input/gene_presence_absence_rtab_pyseer_maf05.tsv \
  --similarity Data_input/phylogeny_similarity.tsv \
  --output-patterns patterns_Glucose_maf05_PA.txt \
  > pyseer_results_Glucose_maf05_PA.txt


pyseer_results_glm_binary_PA.txt


 Pyseer code to run the presence absence data using the binary phenotype where Mucoid is 1 and Dry is 0. We run a generalized linear model. 

pyseer --phenotypes Data_input/Binary_phenotype_pyseer.tsv \
  --pres Data_input/gene_presence_absence_rtab_pyseer_maf05.tsv \
  --distances Data_input/phylogeny_distance_forglm.tsv \
  --max-dimensions 8 \
  --output-patterns patterns_glm_binary_PA.txt \
  > pyseer_results_glm_binary_PA.txt


##### SNP-level variation

Pyseer code to evaluate the association between SNP-level variation with the traits (binary and continuous)

pyseer_results_glm_binary_snps.txt

In the binary phenotype, we ran a generalized linear model where the population structure was accounted for based on the distances stated by the phylogenetic tree

pyseer --phenotypes Data_input/Binary_phenotype_pyseer.tsv \
  --vcf Data_input/strain_118_filtered.recode.vcf.gz \
  --distances Data_input/phylogeny_distance_forglm.tsv \
  --max-dimensions 8 \
  --output-patterns patterns_glm_binary_snps.txt \
  > pyseer_results_glm_binary_snps.txt

pyseer_snp_results_glucose.txt

In the glucose phenotype, the population structure was accounted for as the kinship matrix 


pyseer --lmm --phenotypes Data_input/Glucose_phenotype_pyseer.tsv \
  --vcf Data_input/strain_118_filtered.recode.vcf.gz \
  --similarity Data_input/phylogeny_similarity.tsv \
  --output-patterns patterns_snps_glucose.txt \
  > pyseer_snp_results_glucose.txt
